  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>Pseudancistrus barbatus (Valenciennes, 1840). Common name: Wreath Pleco. Type locality: La Mana River, French Guiana. Size: 200 mm (7.9\") SL.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>South America: Oyapock, Mana, Maroni, Suriname, Corantijn and Essequibo River basins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>Occurs in rapids where it lives in the rocky anfractuosities in the strong current zones. The length of the male snout bristles might be related with the hierarchic level of the individual within the population.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>Pseudancistrus is the only genus of the Ancistrini (former Ancistrinae) that lacks evertible cheek plates. Because of this characteristic, it has at times been placed in the Hypostominae.</p><p>Etymology: Greek, pseudes = false + Greek, agkistron = hook or barb, \"False Ancistrus\". The specific epithet literally means bearded (barbatus = bearded).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1170",
      "html": "<p>Histoire naturelle des poissons v. 15, pp 506.</p>"
    }
  ],
